Chapter: ChaCha20Poly1305
  cites Foreword chapter ChaCha20
  cites Foreword chapter Poly1305
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe

 ChaCha20-Poly1305 AEAD (RFC 8439 section 2.8). The construction that
 TLS 1.3, DTLS 1.3, and WireGuard use where AES hardware is absent --
 which on the MCU class of device is most of the time.

 ChaCha20 alone is a stream cipher: it gives confidentiality and no
 integrity whatsoever, and a stream cipher without a MAC is malleable,
 so an attacker who cannot read the plaintext can still flip chosen
 bits of it. This chapter is what makes ChaCha20 safe to send over a
 wire. Do not reach for chacha20-encrypt directly.

 The one-time Poly1305 key is the first 32 bytes of ChaCha20 block
 zero. The payload is then encrypted from block one, so the key stream
 and the authenticator key never overlap -- and the Poly1305 key is
 fresh per (key, nonce) pair, which is the whole basis of Poly1305's
 security. A repeated nonce under the same key destroys it.

 To chacha20poly1305-encrypt gives ciphertext and a 16-byte tag.
 To chacha20poly1305-decrypt gives plaintext if the tag verifies, None otherwise.

 We say:

Section: Types

  ChaChaPolyResult = record {
    cp-ciphertext : List Integer,
    cp-tag : List Integer
  }

Section: One-Time Key

 Block zero of the key stream, first 32 bytes. RFC 8439 section 2.6.

  chacha-poly-keygen : List Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  chacha-poly-keygen (key) (nonce) =
    cp-take (chacha-words-to-bytes (chacha-block key 0 nonce)) 32

Section: MAC Input

 The authenticated data and the ciphertext are each zero-padded to a
 16-byte boundary, then followed by their two lengths as 64-bit
 little-endian counts. The lengths are what stop an attacker from
 shifting bytes between the AAD and the ciphertext while keeping the
 concatenation -- and therefore the tag -- unchanged.

  chacha-poly-mac-data : List Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  chacha-poly-mac-data (aad) (ct) =
    let a = aad & cp-pad16 (list-length aad)
    in let c = ct & cp-pad16 (list-length ct)
    in a & c & cp-le64 (list-length aad) & cp-le64 (list-length ct)

  chacha-poly-tag : List Integer, List Integer, List Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  chacha-poly-tag (key) (nonce) (aad) (ct) =
    poly1305-mac (chacha-poly-keygen key nonce) (chacha-poly-mac-data aad ct)

Section: Encrypt

  chacha20poly1305-encrypt : List Integer, List Integer, List Integer, List Integer -> ChaChaPolyResult
  chacha20poly1305-encrypt (key) (nonce) (plaintext) (aad) =
    let ct = chacha20-encrypt key nonce plaintext 1
    in ChaChaPolyResult { cp-ciphertext = ct, cp-tag = chacha-poly-tag key nonce aad ct }

Section: Decrypt

 The tag is verified before a single byte of plaintext is produced.
 Decrypt-then-verify would hand an attacker a decryption oracle; this
 is verify-then-decrypt, and the None branch is not an error path to be
 tidied away -- it is the security property.

  chacha20poly1305-decrypt : List Integer, List Integer, List Integer, List Integer, List Integer -> Maybe (List Integer)
  chacha20poly1305-decrypt (key) (nonce) (ciphertext) (aad) (tag) =
    let expected = chacha-poly-tag key nonce aad ciphertext
    in if poly-tags-equal expected tag then Just (chacha20-encrypt key nonce ciphertext 1)
    else None

Section: Helpers

  cp-pad16 : Integer -> List Integer
  cp-pad16 (len) =
    let r = len - (len / 16) * 16
    in if r == 0 then [] else cp-zeros (16 - r) 0 []

  cp-zeros : Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  cp-zeros (n) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else cp-zeros n (i + 1) (list-push acc 0)

  cp-le64 : Integer -> List Integer
  cp-le64 (n) =
    [bit-and n 255, bit-and (bit-shru n 8) 255, bit-and (bit-shru n 16) 255, bit-and (bit-shru n 24) 255,
     bit-and (bit-shru n 32) 255, bit-and (bit-shru n 40) 255, bit-and (bit-shru n 48) 255, bit-and (bit-shru n 56) 255]

  cp-take : List Integer, Integer -> List Integer
  cp-take (xs) (n) = cp-take-loop xs n 0 []

  cp-take-loop : List Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  cp-take-loop (xs) (n) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else cp-take-loop xs n (i + 1) (list-push acc (list-at xs i))
